365
00:26:05,484 --> 00:26:09,384
As opposed to just, oh, we're going to go hunting some stops.

366
00:26:17,708 --> 00:26:25,608
So stop loss hunting occurs when big players engineer short-term price moves to sweep liquidity, triggering stop loss orders.

367
00:26:25,608 --> 00:26:28,808
Why? It's because they want to fill orders without spiking prices.

368
00:26:28,908 --> 00:26:35,208
So they target areas where stops are likely to be below recent lows or above highs.

369
00:26:35,608 --> 00:26:36,908
This creates a burst of orders.

370
00:26:37,708 --> 00:26:40,015
Sells from triggered stop, sell stops or buys

371
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:42,322
from triggered buy stops, which they absorb to

372
00:26:42,322 --> 00:26:45,206
build positions and run the market in the opposite direction.

